{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (90.48%) to Arenicin-1 R: 29%, V: 24%, A=Y: 14%. Activity: active against E. coli (MIC 4.0 uM) and L. monocytogenes (MIC 3.6 uM). The MIC values are comparable to Ar-1 (3.3 and 2.2 uM, respectively). In vitro toxicity: minimal hemolytic concentration (MHC) 11.1 uM, which is higher than that of Ar-1 (MHC 2.9 uM). SAR: linearization of the peptide via iodoacetamidated cysteine did not affect peptide activity clearly but lienar peptide appeared to be less toxic ( Orlov et al., 2019).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "33321960", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Mar Drugs. 2020 Dec 10;18(12):631. doi: 10.3390/md18120631. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04609", "source_id": "AP04609", "source_numeric_id": "04609", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04609", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Antimicrobial Peptide Arenicin-1 Derivative Ar-1-(C/A) as Complement System Modulator.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
